{"id": "2026-11-15-news-iran-drones-target-us-radar-in-bahrain", "date": "2026-11-15", "stream": "news", "headline": "Iran drones target US radar in Bahrain", "summary": "Iran's IRGC claimed a second drone attack in three days on a US site in Bahrain on 15 November; Bahrain said it intercepted the attacks.", "url": "https://www.thenationalnews.com/news/gulf/2026/11/15/bahrain-issues-first-nationwide-alert-in-months-as-iran-claims-attack-on-base-hosting-us-helicopters/", "source_domain": "thenationalnews.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["ongoing"], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 3, "display_body": "Iran's Revolutionary Guards (IRGC) said on Sunday 15 November that they had launched six drones at a US military site in Bahrain, the second attack they have claimed on US assets in the kingdom in three days. Bahrain's armed forces said their air defences \"intercepted and destroyed a number of Iranian aerial attacks\" before they hit anything. The IRGC statement, carried by the Fars news agency, named a US air-defence radar at Riffa Air Base as the target. The Abu Dhabi daily The National describes the target as a base hosting US helicopters. Bahrain's Interior Ministry sent two nationwide alerts about three hours apart, the first around 04:30 local time (02:30 in Switzerland), telling residents to go to the nearest safe location. They were its first nationwide warnings since September. The US military has not yet commented on Sunday's claim. After Friday's claimed attack it said it had shot down two drones, with no damage or injuries. The IRGC also says two tankers hit sea mines on Saturday 14 November while using an \"unauthorised\" route through the Strait of Hormuz; maritime authorities have not confirmed this. Saudi Arabia condemned the attack on Bahrain.", "why": "until Friday, Iran had not claimed an attack on US forces in a Gulf state since early September. A second strike two days later, on the country that hosts the US Navy's Fifth Fleet, points to a renewed campaign against Gulf hosts of US forces rather than a single act of retaliation. The IRGC's account of the target and of the damage has not been independently confirmed.", "thread_id": "2026-11-15-news-iran-drones-target-us-radar-in-bahrain", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-15", "event_date": "2026-11-15", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Iran", "Bahrain", "IRGC", "United States", "Strait of Hormuz"]}
{"id": "2026-11-15-news-yemen-government-forces-quit-bab-al-mandeb", "date": "2026-11-15", "stream": "news", "headline": "Yemen government forces quit Bab al-Mandeb", "summary": "Southern Yemeni forces withdrew from Dhubab and the Bab al-Mandeb area on 15 November as the Saudi-led coalition intercepted Houthi missiles fired at Riyadh.", "url": "https://www.thenationalnews.com/news/mena/2026/11/15/southern-yemeni-forces-withdraw-from-area-near-bab-al-mandab/", "source_domain": "thenationalnews.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Yemeni government-aligned forces said on Sunday 15 November that they were withdrawing from Dhubab and the area overlooking the Bab al-Mandeb strait. They had announced only last month that they had taken it back from the Houthis. Overnight, the Saudi-led coalition said it had shot down two Houthi ballistic missiles fired at Riyadh. The Southern Armed Forces called the move a \"redeployment\" to protect Aden and to help break the Houthi siege of Taiz, carried out with coalition support. The pullback could leave the Iran-backed Houthis holding the high ground over the Red Sea's southern entrance. Coalition spokesman Turki al-Maliki said three drones were also shot down over Saudi Arabia's Eastern region. Saudi authorities say Houthi missiles and drones have killed at least 26 people in the kingdom since Wednesday 23 September. The UN migration agency (IOM) counts more than 340,000 Yemenis displaced since August.", "why": "Bab al-Mandeb is the second chokepoint, after Hormuz, on the Gulf–Europe shipping route. If the Houthis control the coast above it while Iran is disrupting Hormuz, both ends of the Arabian Peninsula are under pressure at the same time.", "thread_id": "2026-11-15-news-yemen-government-forces-quit-bab-al-mandeb", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-15", "event_date": "2026-11-15", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Yemen", "Houthis", "Saudi Arabia", "Bab al-Mandeb"]}
{"id": "2026-11-15-news-kushner-decries-maximalist-ukraine-positions", "date": "2026-11-15", "stream": "news", "headline": "Kushner decries 'maximalist' Ukraine positions", "summary": "US envoy Jared Kushner criticised both sides' publicised maximalist positions after Moscow and Dublin talks, as Ukraine struck a petrochemical complex in Nizhnekamsk.", "url": "https://www.lemonde.fr/international/live/2026/11/15/en-direct-guerre-en-ukraine-l-emissaire-americain-jared-kushner-regrette-la-diffusion-de-positions-maximalistes-apres-les-negociations-avec-l-ukraine-et-la-russie_6810982_3210.html", "source_domain": "lemonde.fr", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "US envoy Jared Kushner, in a post on X reported on Sunday 15 November, criticised the \"maximalist positions proposed by both sides\" that had been made public after his talks with Vladimir Putin in Moscow on Thursday 12 November and with Volodymyr Zelensky in Dublin on Friday 13 November. He did not name Zelensky, who had said hours earlier that Washington had floated NATO membership in exchange for a withdrawal from the Donbas. Kushner said \"several new ideas have emerged\" and that in private \"both sides understand that practical compromises will be necessary\". He added that \"NATO will remain an essential pillar of European security\". He did not confirm or deny the Donbas-for-NATO account. Overnight into Sunday 15 November, Ukraine's General Staff said it hit a synthetic-rubber petrochemical complex and a crude-processing unit at the TAIF-NK refinery in Nizhnekamsk, in Russia's Tatarstan. Local Russian authorities reported three people injured. Zelensky said Russia had launched more than 2,300 attack drones in the past week. He blamed speed limits that SpaceX places on Starshield (its military satellite service) terminals near the front for the failure of Ukrainian interceptor drones to catch Russian Shaheds.", "why": "the US negotiator is now playing down what the Ukrainian president said publicly about the US offer, four days before the Trump–Xi–Putin meeting planned for Thursday 19 November. What Washington actually put on the table remains unclear.", "thread_id": "2026-11-15-news-kushner-decries-maximalist-ukraine-positions", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-15", "event_date": "2026-11-15", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Jared Kushner", "Ukraine", "Russia", "NATO", "Nizhnekamsk"]}
{"id": "2026-11-15-news-australia-philippines-sign-defence-arrangement", "date": "2026-11-15", "stream": "news", "headline": "Australia, Philippines sign defence arrangement", "summary": "Australia and the Philippines signed a Defence Cooperation Arrangement in Manila on 15 November as the 49th ASEAN summit opened.", "url": "https://www.pm.gov.au/media/enhancing-defence-cooperation-and-maritime-security-southeast-asia", "source_domain": "pm.gov.au", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["official PR"], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Australia and the Philippines signed a new Defence Cooperation Arrangement in Manila on Sunday 15 November, as the 49th summit of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN) opened there. Prime Minister Anthony Albanese attended as a guest. The Australian prime minister's office says the arrangement builds on a 1995 memorandum of understanding. It covers maritime awareness and patrols, intelligence-sharing, planning, training, interoperability and defence infrastructure. Canberra is also adding money to a programme that gives regional partners aerial and surface drones and secure communications. Philippine Defence Secretary Gilberto Teodoro said it would make joint action faster and \"strengthen the credibility of our deterrence posture\". The summit runs until Tuesday 17 November. A code of conduct for the South China Sea, which ASEAN has been negotiating with Beijing, is not expected to be agreed there.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-15-news-australia-philippines-sign-defence-arrangement", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-15", "event_date": "2026-11-15", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Australia", "Philippines", "ASEAN", "South China Sea"]}
{"id": "2026-11-15-news-router-overload-caused-us-ground-stop", "date": "2026-11-15", "stream": "news", "headline": "Router overload caused US ground stop", "summary": "US officials said a contractor's router replacement overloaded air-traffic communications at 17 of 22 FAA en route centres, causing the 13 November nationwide ground stop.", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/15/what-forced-the-us-to-ground-all-planes-a-router-switch-we-now-know", "source_domain": "aljazeera.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["world"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "US officials said on Saturday 14 November that Friday's nationwide ground stop of US flights was caused by a contractor's router upgrade, not a cyberattack. More than 5,000 more flights were cancelled on Saturday. Transportation Secretary Sean Duffy said a contractor, L3Harris, was replacing old copper lines with fibre at a remote site. A router there then flooded the air-traffic-control network with \"1,000 connection attempts every four to five seconds\", disrupting communications at 17 of the Federal Aviation Administration's 22 en route centres (the centres that handle high-altitude traffic between airports). Duffy blamed \"contractor error or a faulty piece of equipment\". The FAA safety staff union said the fault was isolated to two routers updated that day. Airlines expect schedules to be back to normal by Sunday evening, 15 November.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-15-news-router-overload-caused-us-ground-stop", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-15", "event_date": "2026-11-14", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["FAA", "L3Harris", "Sean Duffy"]}
{"id": "2026-11-15-news-cape-verde-votes-for-a-president", "date": "2026-11-15", "stream": "news", "headline": "Cape Verde votes for a president", "summary": "Cape Verde holds its presidential election on 15 November, with incumbent José Maria Neves facing Joana Rosa, the first woman to run for the office.", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/15/polls-open-in-cape-verde-in-race-with-first-female-presidential-candidate", "source_domain": "aljazeera.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["politics"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Cape Verde votes for a president on Sunday 15 November. Incumbent José Maria Neves, of the African Party for the Independence of Cape Verde (PAICV), seeks a second term, and Joana Rosa of the Movement for Democracy (MpD) is the first woman to run for the office since independence in 1975. More than 300,000 voters can choose between six candidates. Polls close at 19:00 GMT (20:00 in Switzerland), so no results are in yet. The PAICV won 37 of the 72 parliamentary seats in May, ending ten years of MpD government. Emigration driven by a lack of jobs is the main campaign issue.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-15-news-cape-verde-votes-for-a-president", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-15", "event_date": "2026-11-15", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Cape Verde", "José Maria Neves", "Joana Rosa"]}
{"id": "2026-11-15-news-eu-treaty-vote-slips-to-2028-at-earliest", "date": "2026-11-15", "stream": "news", "headline": "EU treaty vote slips to 2028 at earliest", "summary": "With no Council of States time to reconcile the EU treaty package in the winter session, a popular vote cannot happen before 2028.", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/news/schweiz/europapolitik-abstimmung-zum-eu-vertragspaket-kommt-wohl-fruehestens-2028", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["switzerland", "politics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "A popular vote on the EU treaty package (often called Bilaterals III) cannot now take place before 2028, SRF reported on Saturday 14 November. The Council of States has not scheduled any time in the winter session to settle differences with the National Council. The National Council plans extra sittings to finish its first reading of the package, possibly early in the session's third week. But Council of States president Stefan Engler (The Centre) said the budget, army funding and the Federal Council and Federal Supreme Court elections leave \"no room\" for reconciling the two chambers' versions. The Federal Chancellery told SRF that June 2027 is the last possible vote date before the autumn 2027 federal elections, and that it cannot be met unless Parliament passes the package this winter. SVP campaign manager Manuel Strupler said he was \"relieved\".", "why": "the package, which covers free movement, electricity, health and access to EU programmes, will now hang over the whole 2027 election campaign. For people living and working here, any changes it brings come later than the government's timetable assumed.", "thread_id": "2026-11-15-news-eu-treaty-vote-slips-to-2028-at-earliest", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-15", "event_date": "2026-11-14", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Bilaterals III", "Council of States", "National Council", "Federal Chancellery"]}
{"id": "2026-11-15-news-thun-sniper-ammunition-reached-russia", "date": "2026-11-15", "stream": "news", "headline": "Thun sniper ammunition reached Russia", "summary": "NZZ am Sonntag reports 110,000 Thun-made sniper rounds exported to Slovenia were resold via Kyrgyzstan to Russia in 2022-2023; Seco is looking into it.", "url": "https://www.nzz.ch/schweiz/vom-berner-oberland-nach-moskau-schweizer-scharfschuetzenmunition-gelangt-illegal-nach-russland-ld.10060901", "source_domain": "nzz.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["switzerland", "security"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "About 110,000 rounds of sniper ammunition made in Thun reached Russia after the full-scale invasion of Ukraine, the NZZ am Sonntag reported on Sunday 15 November, based on Russian import registrations dated 30 December 2022 and 5 April 2023. According to the paper, the rounds were exported legally, with State Secretariat for Economic Affairs (Seco) approval, to a Slovenian arms dealer who had promised they would stay in Slovenia. Slovenian defence-ministry documents show he resold them to two Kyrgyz \"hunting supply\" firms. The plant belonged to the federally owned RUAG until Beretta bought it in 2022, and now trades as SwissP Defence. Seco said the calibres count as war material, that it has refused export licences to Russia since 2014, and that it \"is looking into the information\". SwissP said it has never exported to a sanctioned country. The report comes two weeks before the federal vote on Sunday 29 November on loosening the War Material Act. Opponents cite it as proof that re-export controls already leak. Supporters, such as SVP National Councillor Michael Götte, call it a criminal case that no rule can fully prevent.", "why": "the revision on the ballot would make re-export to third countries easier. This case shows where the current system already fails, which is the point the two campaigns disagree on.", "thread_id": "2026-11-15-news-thun-sniper-ammunition-reached-russia", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-15", "event_date": "2026-11-15", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["SwissP Defence", "Seco", "Russia", "War Material Act"]}
{"id": "2026-11-15-news-thousands-march-in-geneva-against-budget-cuts", "date": "2026-11-15", "stream": "news", "headline": "Thousands march in Geneva against budget cuts", "summary": "Several thousand people marched in Geneva on 14 November against the canton's 2027 budget and its roughly CHF 246 million in savings.", "url": "https://www.letemps.ch/suisse/geneve/a-geneve-la-coalition-contre-l-austerite-rassemble-plusieurs-milliers-de-personnes-pour-faire-boule-de-neige-contre-les-coupes-budgetaires", "source_domain": "letemps.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Several thousand people marched in Geneva on Saturday 14 November against the canton's 2027 budget, at the call of a \"Coalition against austerity\" of nearly 40 unions and associations. The budget, presented by the Conseil d'État in September, plans about CHF 246 million in savings, including measures in health and education, some social-assistance benefits, and subsidies to associations and cultural institutions. The march was organised by the public-sector Cartel intersyndical and the Communauté genevoise d'action syndicale (CGAS). It comes as Vaud's public-sector unions are also in a dispute with their canton over its 2027 budget.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-15-news-thousands-march-in-geneva-against-budget-cuts", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-15", "event_date": "2026-11-14", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Geneva", "Cartel intersyndical", "CGAS"]}
